[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is related to a Path Traversal vulnerability, also known as "Tar Slip" or "Zip Slip." This vulnerability occurs because the `tarfile` module, when used to extract archives, can be tricked into writing files outside the intended destination directory. If a malicious tar archive contains file entries with paths that include directory traversal sequences (e.g., `../../malicious_file`) or absolute paths, and the extraction process does not validate or sanitize these paths, the application will extract these files to arbitrary locations on the filesystem. This can lead to overwriting critical system files, placing malicious executables, or gaining unauthorized access to other parts of the file system.

